# Exception: cross-PC memory stores must be synced (conversation history under
# projects/ stays ignored, but the memory/ folder inside it is shared).
# Re-allow each path segment down to the memory files (git won't descend into an
# ignored parent dir, so every intermediate level must be un-ignored first).
# [cC] covers both casings (git matching is case-sensitive; Claude Code has
# created both). The username wildcard keeps this portable across synced PCs.
!projects/
projects/*
!projects/[cC]--Users-*--claude/
projects/[cC]--Users-*--claude/*
!projects/[cC]--Users-*--claude/memory/
!projects/[cC]--Users-*--claude/memory/**
# Linux/macOS global store: cwd ~/.claude -> slug "-home-<user>--claude" (Linux)
# or "-Users-<user>--claude" (macOS). The trailing "--claude" is the discriminator:
# only the global ~/.claude store ends in it; pCloud PROJECT slugs (e.g.
# -home-kita-pCloudDrive-Code-Research-RA) do not, so they stay ignored and never
# leak research memory to the public repo. Leading -* keeps it portable per user.
!projects/-*--claude/
projects/-*--claude/*
!projects/-*--claude/memory/
!projects/-*--claude/memory/**
